# Announcing Peaseblossom: an Oberon-2 compiler, and libraries and programs for it and for voc

This software was developed with the aid of AI.

Peaseblossom's poc is an Oberon-2 compiler with an LLVM backend for Linux, FreeBSD, OpenBSD and NetBSD, and a VAX backend for VAX/VMS 5.5-2. I wrote it largely because I wanted a more modern language than the limited ones on the VAX system I maintain.

With it come libraries: bindings to libfyaml (YAML), FLTK (GUIs) and libtls, plus dates and times, Unix services, sockets and SQL databases. There's also pogemini, a Gemini server written in Oberon-2 and built on those libraries. A few of the projects work with Vishap Oberon (voc) as well. All are BSD 3-Clause licensed.

